{"at":"2026-10-30T21:18:06.795Z","component":"Native and Rust tray quit localization","evidence":["265685d831c00cb2024b024c06206e6157ff901eb44c8a04fa4a7389af763dab","26d0663359e8f27ca9ad941f46fc0025d6a7bb8dcf2c6ef985b2c8faf8dcde2e","3b00ecbf1b3e02f06df93dde52f8d9e4d19d65515af91a8ccc974c7c9f2294a6","809de0308824c86bbe1399589da6aba3a3775acbe5f734684e4a7fe18d0a0df8","a3fe2949b093745bc95e8df0144b7175238cc303c2cdb7cc7546ff6cc49b12c4"],"id":"3dd18c4ad68ea4274eb7e83e324fb11068609087ccae2bd436a5a6cc494d49dc","kind":"lesson","paths":["mail/locales/en-US/messenger/menubar.ftl","mailnews/base/src/nsMessengerWinIntegration.cpp","rust/sys_tray/src/linux/mod.rs","python/l10n/tb_fluent_migrations/completed/bug_2047459_tray_menu_quit.py"],"quotes":[{"id":"3b00ecbf1b3e02f06df93dde52f8d9e4d19d65515af91a8ccc974c7c9f2294a6","text":"system-tray-menuitem-quit ="},{"id":"265685d831c00cb2024b024c06206e6157ff901eb44c8a04fa4a7389af763dab","text":"rv = LocalizeMessage(l10n, \"system-tray-menuitem-quit\"_ns, {},"},{"id":"26d0663359e8f27ca9ad941f46fc0025d6a7bb8dcf2c6ef985b2c8faf8dcde2e","text":"system-tray-menuitem-quit = {COPY_PATTERN(from_path, \"system-tray-menu-quit.label\")}"},{"id":"809de0308824c86bbe1399589da6aba3a3775acbe5f734684e4a7fe18d0a0df8","text":".get_message(\"system-tray-menuitem-quit\")"},{"id":"a3fe2949b093745bc95e8df0144b7175238cc303c2cdb7cc7546ff6cc49b12c4","text":"system-tray-menuitem-quit = {COPY_PATTERN(from_path, \"system-tray-menu-quit.label\")}"}],"repository":"thunderbird","source":{"basis":"Quoted evidence supports the claim; its interpretation still needs current-source checks.","revision":"0b93f0f7a926ed94c8a0646f18b6734ec7cc0f6d","sourceAt":"2026-10-05T22:44:59Z","type":"extraction"},"status":"supported","supersedes":[],"text":"The new system-tray-menuitem-quit is a message value with platform-specific Exit/Quit text. Windows reads that value with LocalizeMessage, and the Linux tray reads message.value before formatting. The migration copies the old system-tray-menu-quit.label pattern to the new value; its archived body is identical. This is a coordinated consumer/resource change, not a global Fluent convention or an executed translation/native menu result.","title":"The shared tray quit message moves from a Fluent attribute to a value","version":1,"visibility":"shared"}
